---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const phone = "+17044696658";
const phoneDisplay = "+1 (704) 469-6658";
---
<Layout title="Central AC Repair Gastonia NC | Full System Repair | acrepairgastonianc.com" description="Expert central AC repair in Gastonia, NC. All major brands — Carrier, Trane, Lennox. Full diagnostics, written estimates. Call +1 (704) 469-6658.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Services / Central AC Repair</p>
      <h1>Central AC Repair in Gastonia, NC</h1>
      <p>Full-system repair for the cooling backbone of Gastonia homes — from coils to blowers to refrigerant recharge.</p>
      <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-white btn-lg">Get a Quote — {phoneDisplay}</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-block">
      <p>Central cooling systems are the backbone of Gastonia home comfort. Our technicians specialize in full-system <strong>Central AC Repair</strong> — condenser and evaporator coil service, blower motor replacement, refrigerant recharge, and electrical component repair — restoring peak efficiency across your entire home.</p>
      <p>We service all major brands: <strong>Carrier, Trane, Lennox, Rheem, Goodman, York, American Standard</strong>, and more. Every visit includes full system diagnostics and a written repair estimate before any work begins.</p>

      <h2>What Central AC Repair Covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Condenser (outdoor unit) diagnostics and repair</li>
        <li>Evaporator coil cleaning and repair</li>
        <li>Blower motor and fan motor replacement</li>
        <li>Capacitor, contactor, and relay service</li>
        <li>Refrigerant pressure testing and recharge</li>
        <li>Ductwork airflow evaluation</li>
        <li>Control board and thermostat integration checks</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why Central Systems Fail in Gastonia</h2>
      <p>Gaston County summers regularly push temperatures past 95°F, with 80+ days above 90°F annually. That sustained load accelerates wear on compressors, capacitors, and motors. Combined with high humidity, systems that are overdue for maintenance or running low on refrigerant fail faster than in milder climates.</p>
      <p>Early symptoms — reduced airflow, short-cycling, rising energy bills — are your chance to fix a $200–$500 problem before it becomes a $2,000+ compressor or system replacement.</p>

      <div class="cta-box">
        <p>Need central AC repair in Gastonia?</p>
        <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
      </div>

      <h2>Related</h2>
      <p><a href="/services/emergency-ac-repair/">Emergency AC Repair</a> · <a href="/services/refrigerant-leak-repair/">Refrigerant Leak Repair</a> · <a href="/services/compressor-repair/">Compressor Repair</a> · <a href="/problems/">Common AC Problems</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
